CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ array deleted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
delete\[\] of non-array object: FAILURE
--
Fixed: CBMC's C library malloc (also calloc, alloca and the contracts
library's fresh objects) cleared __CPROVER_malloc_is_new_array but left
__CPROVER_new_object, the object of the last new-expression, so delete[]
saw that object recorded as not an array (develop too, 8fcda33365).  Seen
in libc++'s ~basic_filebuf for std::ofstream (cvise reduction).
